# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
coverage/

# next.js
.next/
out/

# production
build/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Loose images at the repo root. These are almost always scratch screenshots
# taken while debugging, and for a compliance product they tend to show a real
# organisation's posture and findings. A stray `git add -A` publishing one is
# exactly the disclosure this product exists to prevent.
#
# Root-level only, so genuine assets under public/, docs/ and components/ are
# unaffected. Product imagery belongs in those directories and should be added
# deliberately, with `git add -f` if it ever needs to sit at the root.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.webp
/*.avif

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.bun-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# `deploy/.env` is already matched above, and is called out because it is
# generated rather than hand-written: scripts/stack-env.sh puts this worktree's
# compose project name and port block there, and compose reads it because it
# sits beside compose.yaml (ENT-250). Committing one would give every checkout
# the same ports again, which is the thing that change undid.
deploy/.env

# supabase CLI runtime state (also covered by supabase/.gitignore once ENT-41 lands)
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# vercel
.vercel

# Claude Code per-user settings (skills + agents stay tracked under .agents/)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Kept only so a stray copy cannot be committed by accident. Claude Code does
# NOT read this file: per-user MCP servers live in ~/.claude.json, added with
# `claude mcp add --scope user`. See docs/maintainers.md.
.mcp.local.json

# Playwright MCP per-session artifacts (snapshots + console logs)
.playwright-mcp/

# local scratch space (drafts, generated docs, throwaway experiments)
/scratch/

# Git worktrees are checked out inside the repo; they are separate checkouts and
# must never be staged as files of this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
# Go build artifacts
apps/*/bin/

# go.work IS committed: it is the mechanism joining the service modules, and
# CI resolves intra-repo imports through it. go.work.sum is not. It is a local
# by-product holding hashes already covered by each module's own go.sum, it
# churns on unrelated commands, and CI passes without it.
go.work.sum


# Playwright
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/blob-report/


# Python (ENT-218).
#
# uv.lock IS committed, for the same reason bun.lock and go.sum are: the next
# person's install must resolve what this one did. .venv is not; it is a local
# by-product uv rebuilds from the lock in seconds.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
